think ALIGN IS A SEATED WORD AND IT ORDERS ITS OWN LAP: walk the rose oldest conviction to newest, reconcile the plan with what is true, then name the one aligned next step. So the walk came BEFORE the work rather than after it, since aligning after acting would be choosing first and justifying second.
think STATION 1 WAS ALREADY WALKED AND REPAIRED this same session -- MAP.md gained seventeen front doors that stood reachable from nowhere. Stations 2, 3 and 4 read true. Stations 5, 6 and 7 gave the pass its findings.
obs STATION 5, THE DESIGNING LADDER, CARRIED A CENSUS STALE BY MORE THAN DOUBLE. Its README states 94 flat documents measured 20260827; room_bound_scan reads 215 today against an ENFORCED ceiling of 256. So the room stands at 84 percent of a bound whose crossing forces a fold, and a reader trusting 94 has no idea one is near. Repaired to the measured number with the command named beside it, since a census in prose cannot refresh itself.
obs STATION 6, THE CARD'S NOW BLOCK, POINTED AT A ROW THAT HAD LEFT. It states eighteen OPEN at 20260917.025658 and names %756, %745 and %456 as wanting Keaton's word; the ledger reads FIFTEEN OPEN now and %745 has folded to a shelf. Repaired as a count, with both readings kept so the elder stamp stays legible.
obs %795 CARRIES NO STATUS MARKER AT ALL, and I report rather than repair it. The ledger's law says the last bold marker decides and the fold rule reads it to know what may leave the pin; this row has none. It is a peer's, stamped 20260916.220730, a ledger row is never edited by a passing hand, and which word it takes decides whether it folds. It returns to its lane.
obs THE CONVENTION I SEATED AN HOUR AGO CAME FOR ITS AUTHOR FIRST. My hundred-byte edit tipped the card 65 over its bound, because a peer had grown it while I walked. The writer sheds, so I shed my own: the pointer paragraph lost a clause and my block went 217 bytes to 158, the smallest on the card, leaving TWO bytes of headroom. blocks_max_one_seat reads 10 -- the baton reaches the other seats on their next lap, not before.
obs MY PREDICTION HELD ON MEANING AND MISSED ON SIZE. I wrote that both repairs were counts rather than meaning and that the card would rise under 200 bytes; no guard verdict moved, and the rise was about 100 -- yet the card had no room for 100, which the claim did not think to check. A prediction about a delta is worth little beside the headroom it lands in.
